From: nvb-uy <105564560+nvb-uy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] comdlg32: Drive the portal from a hidden Explorer file dialog.

GetOpenFileName and GetSaveFileName create their dialog as usual but keep it hidden and show the portal instead, with the dialog's title, folder, name and file types. The choice is typed into the hidden dialog and accepted, so hooks, templates, CDN_FILEOK, default extensions, overwrite checks and the ANSI structures behave exactly as with the visible dialog; when the hook refuses the file the portal comes back. A hooked or templated dialog only does this with the always policy.
---
diff --git a/dlls/comdlg32/filedlg.c b/dlls/comdlg32/filedlg.c
--- a/dlls/comdlg32/filedlg.c
+++ b/dlls/comdlg32/filedlg.c
